# Build context exclusions for the server image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `server/Dockerfile`'s build context is this directory,
# and Docker uploads the whole context to the daemon before building. Without
# these lines that includes `target/` - measured at ~1 GB on this repo - plus any
# stray database file, which turns a 5-second context transfer into a minute and
# can push a hosted builder over its context limit. Nothing here is needed to
# compile the binary.

# Build artefacts. Rebuilt inside the builder stage from the lockfile.
target/

# A local SQLite database and its WAL sidecars are STATE, not source. Copying one
# into an image would bake a developer's ledger into the deployed artefact - the
# single worst thing this file prevents.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Secrets and local overrides. `.env` is gitignored for the same reason; an
# image must never contain one, and a context that carries it is a context that
# could land in a layer.
.env
.env.*

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp

# Documentation is not needed to build, and the config it might describe is
# copied explicitly and deliberately rather than swept in.
*.md
